title: 'SpecBuilder wipes a modeled (inline-struct) spec: spec_set/spec_merge on AgentSandbox
  Sandbox serialise spec as {}'
updated: 2026-09-03T05:04:18Z
---

Reproduced 2026-09-03 on master (1.108):

  my $k=IO::K8s->new(with=>["IO::K8s::AgentSandbox"]);
  my $s=$k->new_object("Sandbox", metadata=>{name=>"x",namespace=>"d"}, spec=>{shutdownPolicy=>"Retain"});
  $s->spec_set("shutdownPolicy","Delete");
  print $s->to_json;   # spec is {} -- Retain is gone, Delete never arrived

Cause: SpecBuilder (applied to every CRD class by IO::K8s::APIObject) assumes spec is a plain hashref. On a class whose spec is an inline struct (k8s spec => { ... }), ref($self->spec) is the _Spec object, so spec_set does `$spec = {}; $self->spec($spec)` -- the writer coerces that empty hash into a fresh _Spec object and the subsequent write lands in the now-orphaned hash. spec_get returns undef for the same reason. spec_merge shows the same loss.

Affects the 8 AgentSandbox classes today and every provider class that gets a modeled spec later. Builder roles (CertManaged, HelmManaged, MiddlewareBuilder, the cilium branch of NetworkPolicy) share the hash-only assumption.

Found during the CRD design grill; resolution shape is being decided there (object-aware SpecBuilder vs. no SpecBuilder on modeled classes).
